    "updated_at": "2021-02-26T22:34:49Z",
    "body": "Supporting a BYOB reader for on the `ReadableStream` will avoid the buffer allocation issues as you'll be able to append bytes directly from the underlying source to an existing buffer.\r\n\r\nThe `bulkRead()` method proposed in whatwg/streams#1003 would also allow you to specify a timeout but that has the same questions about semantics as passing an `AbortSignal` to `read()` being discussed in whatwg/streams#1103.",
